
hi =)

can you review the staged UTF-8 fixes for double encoding issues encountered
in the coding zenka and file reading | writing tools if something was
forgotten to address ?

you are invited to test the available tools for UTF-8 compliance, but should
not worry about already written files that appear mis-encoded, because the
fix is being introduced just now, and prior written content was not been
adressed yet.

and especially, also test your notes system. it was confirmed having double
encoding issues, so it will have such content still, but any new notes
written, listed or read should no longer have the issue since the staged
file.read fixes.

here are the main read and write operations in context [ regular perl open
based ones have not been searched for yet, if you want you can do that also
in the src/coding.* namespace and assess the code for how it would treat
and pass through UTF-8 content]

